"notes": [
"A's 8-bar outro is drums-only; B's 8-bar intro too \u2192 16-bar long blend: B in at A 1:02 (bar 33, on the phrase) from B 0:00, swap the bass on the 1 of bar 9 (A 1:17), A out by the end of its 8-bar loop.",
"In phrases: bars 1\u20138 bring B in with its lows killed behind a gentle filter (fader up over 4 bars, highs opening, mids held 4 dB down until the swap); from bar 9 both ride together while the last 8 bars take A out \u2014 highs, then mids, then the fader \u2014 under a slowly rising high-pass; A's reverb swells over its last 2 bars and its echo over the last, both still fed a beat past the cut so they ring over B. B's high-pass builds, resonant, over the 2 bars before its lows drop in on bar 9 and lets go on that 1.",
"B's intro is stretched: B loops its bars 1\u20138 (8 bars) from B 0:00 as it comes in and releases the loop on the 1 of bar 9 (a phrase), so its intro then runs as A leaves.",
"A's outro is stretched: A's music runs out 8 bars before the blend ends, so from bar 9 A loops its bars 33\u201340 (8 bars, 1:02) until it leaves on the phrase.",
"B is pitched -1.6% to A's 124.0 BPM through the blend (key lock on), then the tempo drifts to B's own 126.0 BPM over 32 bars once A is out."
